  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n[The rules for choosing a navigable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#the-rules-for-choosing-a-navigable) uses a non-existent `targetNavigable` variable in step 11 of the \"If the user agent has been configured such that in this instance it will create a new [top-level traversable](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#top-level-traversable)\" part of step 8:\n\n> 11. Set targetNavigable's [is created by web content](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#is-created-by-web-content) to true.\n\nI think this should instead use `chosen`, which is the navigable that's just been created.",
